      },
      "inLanguage": "en-GB",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-1",
          "name": "Which Range Rover models use the 2.2 diesel engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The 2.2 litre diesel engine, badged TD4 or SD4, was fitted to the Range Rover Evoque built between 2011 and 2018. It shares its 224DT engine block with other Land Rover models from the same era, though the Evoque remains the version we're asked about most."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-2",
          "name": "Is the Range Rover Evoque 2.2 TD4 engine reliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can be reliable with consistent servicing, but as these vehicles age, EGR, DPF and turbo-related faults become more common. Reliability at this point depends heavily on maintenance history, mileage and whether known wear items like the timing belt have been replaced on schedule."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-3",
          "name": "What are the common faults with the 2.2 diesel Evoque engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The most frequently reported issues are EGR valve contamination, DPF blockages from repeated short journeys, and turbo wear causing whistling noises or a loss of power. Timing belt condition is also worth checking, since this engine uses a belt rather than a timing chain."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-4",
          "name": "What's the difference between the TD4 and SD4 tune?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Both use the same 2.2 litre 224DT engine block, but the SD4 is tuned for higher power output than the TD4. In practice this affects performance rather than the fundamental reliability concerns, which are broadly similar across both tunes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-5",
          "name": "How much does a Range Rover 2.2 engine replacement cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cost depends on whether a repair, reconditioned engine or full replacement is appropriate, along with the extent of any damage found. We assess each vehicle individually and provide a clear, itemised quote once diagnosis is complete rather than a fixed headline price."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-6",
          "name": "Is it worth replacing the engine on an older Evoque?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "This depends on the vehicle's mileage, condition and current value compared with the cost of repair or replacement. We'll talk through the realistic options honestly, including whether a targeted repair could resolve the fault without a full engine change."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-7",
          "name": "Do reconditioned 2.2 diesel engines come with a warranty?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, reconditioned and replacement engines are supplied with warranty cover. We'll confirm the specific terms for your engine before any work is booked, so you know exactly what's included."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.2#faq-question-8",
          "name": "What areas do you cover for Range Rover engine work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We're based in Grays, Essex, and regularly support customers across Essex, London and the wider South East, alongside UK-wide enquiries for engine supply and fitting. Get in touch to confirm availability for your location."
          }
        }
      ]
